      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-04-06_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>WM. M'CLI4]AN &amp; SONS,</head>
        <p>WM. M'CLI4]AN &amp; SONS,</p>
        <p>MONAGHAN. :IRELAND DEALERS IN FIRST-CLAUS IRISH HUNTERS AND CARRIAGE HOIISBS AND JOB MASTURS. We beg to thank the Gentry of Liverpool and surrounding districts for their past pltrnnage since opening'our LIVERPOOL BRANCH': SANDON MEWS, 80, EGERTON ST. Where owing to the increasing demand for our Speciality in High-class Carriage and Hunting Horses, and to supply this demand we have completed extensive alterations, and trust, by strict and personal supervision of business, to retain the confidence in the future as in the past of our numerous Patrons. Also soliciting the favour of those in want of good, Sound, High-class Irish t I °roes, at moderate pricss.to entrust us with their requirements, our sole aim being attention and entire satisfaction in our dealings with customers.</p>
        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY OP CHESTER will be held at the COURT ROUSE, KNUTSFORD, in and for tlae said County, on MONDAY, the Bth day of April next, at E!even o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury Will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincham, Bucklow, Dareshury, Dukinfield, Middlewich, Sandbach, Congleton, North- Prestbury, and Stockport,forming the Knutsford Dtstrict, and the trials of all prisoners committed from slich Divisions, will take place at such Sessions. The Vrand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must he in attendance at the Conrt House, Knutsford, at the cn,ening of the Court on MONDAY, the Bth day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the Castle of CHESTER, on WEDNESDAY, the 10th day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing ec all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Broxton, Chester Castle, Eddisbury, Nant- "'icily Runcorn. Winsford, and Wirral, forming the Clp2.ster District, and the trials of all prisoners corn- nutted from the last-mentioned Divisions will take Place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attend- Ince at the Castle of Chester, at the Opening of the k..-ieurt on WEDNESDAY, the 10th day of April next, at 41even o'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Chester, 18th March, 1907.</p>
