        <p>A hen belonging to Mr. W. S. Howard, Grove of gentlemen interested' in the Infirmary extension ! The fortnightly meeting of the Runcorn - Board ch Rouse, Fearnhead, yesterday laid a large egg which movement was held in the Council Chamber at the Guardians was held at Dutton on Tuesday. Alderman Ott being opened was found to contain another egg. 1 Town Hall on Thursday, to appoint committees and Norman presided, and there were also present :—Rev. C. R. Nunn, Messrs. T. Baxter, S. Woodward, T. Wright, * * * i workers to, make arrangements in connection with the It is reported that "the health of King Leopold of grand bazaar and fete which is to be held at mid- &amp;11.eLe Lnjaki(33eral.tv73f.GM;rei:,teJe. ,IkoeuAlearteeT. TWosodr,eePe. Belgium-is giving rise to considerable anxiety among summer in the beautiful grounds of .Mr. Henry H. Eyes', W. Harriso'n, W. Egerton G. Pilling,' T. Agtwis, bis entourage." We wonder if there is the same con- Greenall, Hill Cliffe. Mr. W. Peter Rylands occupied T. Guest, H. M. Davies, J. H. Davies, G- F. Ashton tern in the Congo ?- I the chair. The several sub-committees were appointed, (clerk), W. E. Hough (assistant clerk), T. Cook, J. I and they will enter upon their duties in the course of Pearson, and W. R. de Prez (relieving officers), and J. , the next few days. The proceeds will go to the fund Cunnah (master). The House Committee intimated their thanks to Mr, for the enlargement of the Infirmary, and the good J. W. Temperley for presentjog buns to the whole of cause and the enjoyable function Should combine to the inmates of the House on Good Friday. There were make the undertaking a great social and financial in the House 164 persons as against 142 twelve months success. i ago. • 1 PREMIER CYCLES with Stnrmey Archer three Mr. Woodward moved, Mr. Wright seconded and Mr. . I 1 speed gear, nine guineas. Two speed gear eight . Morris supported a vote of thanks to the chairman and I vice-chairman for their services durin