sses were: Miss Annie Horobin, champagne delaine with .hat to match, and Miss M. Chesworth, brown cloth braide and velvet cream hat, and both carried bouquets of daffodils. Mr. Horobin's best man was his brother, Master A. C. Gibson, whilst Mr. Lincoln Gibson per- formed a similar office for his brother. Later in the day the newly married couples left for the honeymoon Jr. and Mrs. Gibson proceeding to North Wales, whilst Mr. and Mrs. Horobin went to St. Annes, both briies travelling in blue costumes with hats to match. Many handsome presents were received.</p>
