        <p>A LONG TIME DEAD. Resting on beams near the roof of a barn adjoining the Old Castle Inn, Stevenage, Herta, is the coffin of a former landlord, Henry Trigg, who died about 1722, and expressed the following curious wish in his will: " And as to my body, I commit it to the west end of my hovel to be decently laid there upon a floor erected by my executor upon the purloyne."</p>
