        <p>The Works Competition. The second round of the Warrington Works competi tion commences this afternoon, when two matches will be decided on the Wilderspool ground. The draw for this stage has resulted as follows :—Crosfields v. Stockton Heath and London and North-Western v. St. Helens Cable Co. (to-day), Corporation v. Wilderspool (Monday),Ryland's v. Orford Tannery (Tuesday) White- cross v. Monks Hall (Wednesday), E•lelsten's v. Castle Rubber (Thursday), Fletcher Russell v. Richmonds (Friday), anc Walker's Brewery v. Wyman's (Monday April 15th). The ties in the first round this week resulted as follows ;—Wilderspool 13, Naylor's 11 ; Corporation Employees 9, Longford Wire 3 ; Whitecross 32, Perrin's 7 ; Rylands 41,Monks Hall 0; Castle Rubber 16, Robertson 6 ; Monks Hall 6, Garton's 0. In the second round to-day's games will commence at 3.30, whilst in the evening fixtures, the kick-off is fixed for 6.15. Marriages. FORSTER,—FoRD—March 30th at the Parish Church, Warrington, by the Rev. T. 30th, Barber, Alfred Forster to Mary Jane Ford. WlLLlAms—Cnoss—March 30th, at the Parish Church, Warrington,by the Rev. Canon Willis, Ernest Williams to Ethel Emma i,ross. CALLON—WRIGHT—March 30th, at the Parish Church, Warrington, by the Rev. Canon Willis, John Callon to Margaret Harrison Wright. How:I-nix—CITES 4th,at the Parish Church, Warrington, by the Rev. Canon Willis, Charlie Horobin to Martha Chesworth. G 113 SON—C 1-1 ES ORTH—April 4th, at the Parish Church, Warrington, by the Rev. Canon Willis, Harry Robinson Gibson to Mary Jane Cheaworth. WALMSLEY—WAKEFIELD—ApriI 4th, at the Parish Church,Warringcon, by the Rev. Canon Willis, Arthur Perrins Waltnsley to Mary Ellen Wakefield.</p>
